# nova — real-world examples

> The `nova` CLI is legacy OpenStack — the unified `openstack` client replaces it (see table).

## List VMs

```sh
nova list                    # current tenant
nova list --all-tenants      # all tenants (admin only)
```

## Boot a VM on a specific host

```sh
nova boot --nic net-id=<net_id> \
          --image <image_id> \
          --flavor <flavor> \
          --availability-zone nova:<host_name> <vm_name>
```

## Stop and start a server

```sh
nova stop <server>
nova start <server>
```

## Attach a network interface to a VM

```sh
nova interface-attach --net-id <net_id> <server>
```

| Legacy nova         | Unified client            |
| ------------------- | ------------------------- |
| nova list           | openstack server list     |
| nova boot           | openstack server create   |
| nova stop / start   | openstack server stop / start |
